On the client machine **after** installing the nfs server 

install nfs-commons using apt on client
```sudo apt install nfs-common```  
check using ```showmount -e <ip-address-of-server>```  
This should list the exports exported by the server  
next create a folder e.g. ```/mnt/rpi_folder```  
and mount the nfs-servers folder to the newly created ```rpi_folder``` using  
```sudo mount <ip-of-nfs-server>:/exports/nfs  /mnt/rpi_folder```  

now any editing of the rpi_folder is reflected under the nfs_servers exported folder.